@startuml
title Agent Claim / Release — Approved Preconditions and Atomic Audit
actor Agent
participant "Agent workspace" as UI
participant "AgentDisputeController" as C
participant "DisputeService" as S
database PostgreSQL as DB
Agent -> UI : Claim case / release with reason
UI -> C : POST claim or release + If-Match + JWT
C -> S : Authenticated agent; validate command
S -> DB : Load dispute in mutation transaction
alt Missing If-Match
  S --> C : 428 / 2007
else Malformed If-Match
  S --> C : 400 / 1004
else Stale version
  S --> C : 412 / 2006
else Invalid state / assignment with current version
  S --> C : 409 / 2005
else Valid command
  group One transaction: guarded state change and event
    alt Claim OPEN / unassigned
      S -> DB : Conditional UNDER_REVIEW, agent, assigned_at, version + 1
    else Release UNDER_REVIEW assigned to caller
      S -> DB : Conditional OPEN, clear agent + assigned_at, version + 1
    end
    alt Guarded write succeeded
      S -> DB : Append CLAIMED / RELEASED event with resulting disputeVersion
      S -> DB : Commit
      S --> C : 200 refreshed agent detail + new strong ETag
    else Lost write race
      S -> DB : Rollback; no event committed
      S --> C : 412 / 2006
    end
  end
end
C --> UI : HTTP status + JSON envelope + X-Correlation-ID
note over UI, DB
Approved: action preconditions use the parent agent-detail ETag.
Release requires nonblank internal reason; no customer disclosure.
Responses include boolean request status and numeric error_code.
end note
@enduml
